{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790513084,"nonce":"nwYSkNeVQdMCMFmK55ynKZ3TN/Y=","message":"2026-09-27, confirmed with ash-b7 (Ash 501f8a5). On wasm, a collection inside an allocation isn't safe. The ash_std Rust frame that asked for memory holds pointers in wasm engine locals, which the shadow-stack scan doesn't reach, and only compiled Haxe pins its registers into memory. Production wasm programs already collect this way at TLAB refills, on Ash's heap and on caribou's, and are saved only because collections are rare. Ash's own AOT stress never collected at all (the constants scan root sets safepoint_mode), so its passing said nothing.\n\nDesign, for scheduling with the user. Split: caribou's crates/caribou/src/heap/immix.rs is ours, Ash's std/src/gc.rs is ash-b7's.\n1. On wasm, a due trigger in an allocation (refill or slow path) defers and bumps the poll epoch on every deferral. Done: the poll request, plus heap::poll_safepoint called from sched::poll (d230d66).\n2. A runtime-depth count. ash_std functions that call back into compiled code (sort comparators, closures run by the runtime, hl.Api, the fiber body runner, HostLink after/init into Haxe, WrenLift calling a Haxe export) increment it around the call. poll_safepoint defers while it is nonzero. This needs Ash: a seam slot, or an ash_std counter the heap can read.\n3. Allocation entry points called directly from compiled code (hlp_alloc_obj, alloc_bytes, alloc_array, ...) are safepoints when the depth is zero, since every frame below is compiled and pinned. This restores real per-allocation stress coverage for compiled allocations, and it fixes code that never polls (recursion without loops, long runtime phases).\n4. The hard-pressure backstop on wasm grows memory first and collects in place only when growth fails, and it reports under ASH_GC_STATS when it fires.\nUntil 2 and 3 exist, moving refill collections to polls would only trade one hazard for another (a poll inside a runtime callback), so caribou's refill is unchanged for now.","files":null}]}